{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-17330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the expression ${[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})]}^{16}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-17330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=16$ and $\\phi =\\frac{\\theta }{2}.$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})]}^{16} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(16\\cdot \\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(16\\cdot \\frac{\\theta }{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-17330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6199eba06847c018b837b33428f676b63ad1d8011e40c269e6a415b0d90088ce"} {"question" "q-17330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-17330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "16[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})]"] ["math" "16[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\theta }{2})]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(16\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(16\\theta )]"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-17330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-104123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the expression $\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{3}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-104123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{3}}=[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{-3}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\phi ]^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-3$ and $\\phi =5\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{3}} & =[\\operatorname{cos}⁡5\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5\\theta ]^{-3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(-3)\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5(-3)\\theta ) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-15\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-15\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-15\\theta )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-104123" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6199eba06847c018b837b33428f676b63ad1d8011e40c269e6a415b0d90088ce"} {"question" "q-104123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-104123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )]"] ["math" "15[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ]"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta )"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\theta }{5})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\theta }{5})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\theta }{3})-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\theta }{3})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-104123" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(15\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(15\\theta )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-325322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the expression $\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{10}}.$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{10}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-325322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{10}}={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-10}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-10$ and $\\phi =\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{10}} & ={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-10} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-10\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-10\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-10\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-10\\theta )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10\\theta ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-325322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6199eba06847c018b837b33428f676b63ad1d8011e40c269e6a415b0d90088ce"} {"question" "q-325322" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-325322" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\cos(10\\theta)-i\\sin(10\\theta)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-325325" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify the expression $\\frac{3}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{4}},$ where $x$ and $y$ are functions of $\\theta .$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\frac{3}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{4}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-325325" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{4}}=3{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-4}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-4$ and $\\phi =\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{4}} & =3{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-4} \\\\  & =3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-4\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-4\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-4\\theta )]=3[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-325325" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6199eba06847c018b837b33428f676b63ad1d8011e40c269e6a415b0d90088ce"} {"question" "q-325325" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-325325" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\cos(4\\theta)-3i\\sin(4\\theta)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-325346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{4}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]^{5}}$ in the form $x+\\text{i}y,$ where $x$ and $y$ are functions of $\\theta .$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\frac{4}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]^{5}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-325346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}^{5}} & =4{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}^{-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-5$ and $\\phi =4\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}^{-5} & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5\\cdot 4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-5\\cdot 4\\theta )] \\\\  & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-20\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-20\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-20\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-20\\theta )] & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(20\\theta )-[-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\theta )]] \\\\  & =4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(20\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n4{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )]}^{-5}=4[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(20\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(20\\theta )].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/state.json" "file_sha256" "9f7cecbc08d66f41aac11b6f48d17f6858c23b60df101e005112cee96ec03b3b"} {"question" "q-325346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6199eba06847c018b837b33428f676b63ad1d8011e40c269e6a415b0d90088ce"} {"question" "q-325346" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063848/stat